### Prerequisites, not source ###
# A memory is Monty's pretrained model, exported to the format this application
# reads — a hundred megabytes of it, and the same kind of thing as the YCB
# meshes: it arrives through `/prerequisites`, which exports it, and it never
# comes through `git`. Everything under `libraries/` goes, at any depth, and the
# `README.md` that explains the layout stays.
/priv/monty/libraries/*
!/priv/monty/libraries/README.md

# The file a fetch streams into before its checksum matches and it is renamed
# into place. A killed download left one in the tree once and `git status`
# offered it up.
*.part

# The roots a downloader is pointed at when they are inside the checkout
# (`MONTY_DATA`, `MONTY_MODELS`, `MONTY_LOGS`), the drafts the builder saves, and
# the wandb directory a run writes beside whatever started it.
/priv/tbp/
/priv/data/
/priv/experiments/
/priv/wandb/

# A database kept in a file, with the two sidecars SQLite writes beside it.
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm

/tmp/

